{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3182","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3182","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3182\",\"parent_revision\":\"c15fce8c16243afe43c3c42a46dac6fe4e74cd0f\",\"root_revision\":\"8d6d511f9b31c922774f61a3c27842d4c91609ad668155452ee6bb985b79edc9\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-23\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`backlog_add` can complete with `item_ref: \\\"\\\"` \u2014 no GitHub issue created \u2014 while returning a success-shaped result. The caller receives a populated dict and no error.\\n\\nObserved in CI on `main`, run 32624257966, job \\\"Python / E2E live tests\\\":\\n\\n```\\nplugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py:196: in test_l1_add_with_real_issue\\n    assert item_ref.startswith(\\\"#\\\"), f\\\"Expected item_ref like '#N', got: {item_ref!r}\\\"\\nE   AssertionError: Expected item_ref like '#N', got: ''\\n\\nplugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py:318: in test_l11_resolve_alternative_end\\n    l11_issue_num = int(create_result[\\\"item_ref\\\"].lstrip(\\\"#\\\"))\\nE   ValueError: invalid literal for int() with base 10: ''\\n```\\n\\nTwo symptoms, one defect. The remaining lifecycle tests then skip on the `l1_ok` sentinel, and two more pass only because they assert types rather than values.\\n\\nWhy the cause is still unknown, which is the substance of this item: `operations._try_create_github_issue` (around line 1377) returns `None` on either `try_get_github(...) is None` (\\\"GitHub unavailable\\\") or a caught `GithubException`/`BacklogError` (\\\"Issue creation failed: {e}\\\"). Both are recorded only via `out.warn(...)`. The reason therefore lives in `result[\\\"warnings\\\"]`, and neither test assertion includes it, so roughly four weeks of CI logs contain no information about why creation failed.\\n\\nThis is the failure shape `.claude/rules/silent-failure-prevention.md` prohibits directly: a write operation that does not report what changed, and a branch on an input condition whose fallback neither acts nor errors. An agent calling `backlog_add` cannot distinguish \\\"issue created\\\" from \\\"issue not created, item exists locally only\\\".\\n\\nNot caused by any recent change. Verified independently: every Code Quality run on `main` back through 2026-08-20 failed, including commits well before the recent backlog_core work (58df37b85, 79962289b, d22c524e6, 0a2ca9177). A subagent sampled e2e job conclusions on `main` on 2026-07-28, 08-06, 08-10 through 08-13, and every run from 08-14 to 08-23 \u2014 all failure, zero successes, so at least four weeks.\\n\\nThe symptom text changed once without the defect changing. Before 2026-08-18 it read `Expected item_ref in result, got: [...]` with `'reference': 'p1-mcp-test-<uuid>-live-test-item'` \u2014 the local-only fallback. PR #3160 made `item_ref` always present, so it became `got: ''`. Same bug throughout.\\n\\nRuled out as causes, with evidence: not a flake (20+ consecutive identical failures; the fixture uses a fresh tmp dir, a per-run UUID prefix and `force=True`); not rate limiting or auth rejection (step completes in 12.4s, no 403 or 429); not leftover state; not run contention. The job's token carries `Issues: write`.\\n\\nUser-provided context: a subagent's suggested cheapest first move is to include `result[\\\"warnings\\\"]` and `result[\\\"errors\\\"]` in the test assertion message, so the next CI run reports the actual cause \u2014 but that is a diagnostic aid, and the defect to fix is that a failed create is not surfaced to the caller at all. Whether the right contract is raising, an explicit status field, or something else is design work for grooming.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T00:44:22.114047Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: backlog_add returns an empty item_ref when issue creation fails, and the reason reaches no caller\\nDate: 2026-09-04\\nGoal: Make backlog_add surface why issue creation failed instead of returning a success-shaped empty item_ref.\\nConditions:\\n1. Defect is still present in current code \u2014 `_try_create_github_issue`/`_try_create_backend_issue_ref` (operations.py:1444-1499) record failure only via `out.warn()` | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. `BacklogAddResponse` already has an unused `error: str | None` field (tool_responses.py:216) designed for exactly this signal, left `None` on this path | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Repo convention for this exact shape is documented in rules/silent-failure-prevention.md: \\\"if no fallback action is possible, raise or warn\\\" | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. Blast radius of populating `error`/changing the empty-string contract \u2014 which CLI, MCP, and test callers key off `item_ref == \\\"\\\"` today | Status: DERIVABLE\\n5. Whether the beads-backend sibling path (string-ID branch of `_try_create_backend_issue_ref`) shares the identical silent-failure shape | Status: DERIVABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 3\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 0\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Diagnosed from the E2E live tests failure on main, 2026-08-23\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d74a4bb71b10ca903f738fba60b40b9ae4aaa4874bf6bc99c1b5eb967a8a6cef\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdrCPw\"}"}